.\" Manpage for ~/.config/bob/config.conf
.TH BOB.CONF 5 "2026-08-30" "BOB 0.14.1" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
bob.conf \- BOB user configuration file
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I ~/.config/bob/config.conf
.PP
.I /root/.config/bob/config.conf
(when invoked as actual root without
.BR SUDO_USER )
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bob
reads its persistent user-side configuration from
.IR ~/.config/bob/config.conf .
The file is a flat
.B key=value
text format with one entry per line. Lines starting with
.B #
are comments. Order does not matter.
.PP
When invoked via
.BR sudo ,
.B bob
honors
.B SUDO_USER
and resolves the path against the invoking user's home, not
.IR /root/ .
The file is owned by that user with mode
.BR 0600 .
.PP
The file is created by the first-launch wizard
.RB ( \-\-reconfigure
re-runs it). It is safe to edit by hand.
.
.SH KEYS
.SS Custom service ports
For any service in
.B bob
's registry whose
.B config_key
declares a user-config key (e.g.
.IR ssh_port " for SSH), add a line:"
.PP
.RS
.EX
ssh_port = 2222
.EE
.RE
.PP
Multi-port services use comma-separated values:
.PP
.RS
.EX
samba_ports = 445/tcp, 139/tcp
.EE
.RE
.SS Log directory
.TP
.B log_dir = \fIPATH\fR
Directory where
.B \-d
writes detailed audit reports. Default:
.I ~/.local/share/bob/logs/
(under the invoking user, even via sudo).
.SS SUID whitelist (since v0.3.2)
.TP
.B suid_whitelist = \fIPATTERN[,PATTERN,...]\fR
Comma-separated
.BR fnmatch (3)
patterns matched against the
.B basename
of detected SUID binaries. Matched binaries are suppressed from the
"unexpected SUID" warning. Useful on Kali / pentesting distros that ship
extra SUID tools intentionally.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.EX
suid_whitelist = kismet_cap_*, my_custom_tool
.EE
.RE
.PP
A summary INFO finding
.RI ( suid_audit.whitelisted )
reports the count of suppressed paths so the whitelist is never silent.
.SS Webhook (optional)
.TP
.B webhook_url = \fIURL\fR
Default webhook URL for
.BR \-\-webhook
(overridden by an explicit flag on the command line).
.TP
.B webhook_format = \fIFMT\fR
One of
.BR auto " (default), "
.BR generic ", "
.BR slack .
.
.SH EMAIL ADDRESS BOOK
.B bob
keeps a separate
.I ~/.config/bob/emails
file (also mode 0600) for the email-store wizard used by
.BR \-\-install\-cron .
One address per line, comment lines start with
.BR # .
This is NOT part of
.IR config.conf .
.
.SH RELATED FILES
See
.BR bob (1)
section
.B FILES
for the full list of paths
.B bob
reads or writes under
.IR ~/.config/bob/ .
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bob (1),
.BR bob-profile (5).
